<div class="matrix-info">
  <h4 class="card-title mb-3">What is the Popularity vs. Profitability Matrix?</h4>
  <p class="fs-6 text-muted">The <strong>Popularity vs. Profitability Matrix</strong> helps you analyze your menu items based on <strong>sales performance and profitability</strong>. It categorizes each item into one of four groups:</p>

  <ul class="list-unstyled d-grid gap-2 mb-4">
    <li class="d-flex align-items-center">
      <span class="badge bg-success-subtle text-success me-2 rounded-circle p-1">
        <i class="ti ti-star-filled fs-4"></i>
      </span>
      <strong>Stars</strong> – High sales & high profit (your best items)
    </li>
    <li class="d-flex align-items-center">
      <span class="badge bg-info-subtle text-info me-2 rounded-circle p-1">
        <i class="ti ti-rocket fs-4"></i>
      </span>
      <strong>Plowhorses</strong> – High sales, low profit (optimize pricing or costs)
    </li>
    <li class="d-flex align-items-center">
      <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning me-2 rounded-circle p-1">
        <i class="ti ti-puzzle fs-4"></i>
      </span>
      <strong>Puzzles</strong> – Low sales, high profit (improve marketing & visibility)
    </li>
    <li class="d-flex align-items-center">
      <span class="badge bg-danger-subtle text-danger me-2 rounded-circle p-1">
        <i class="ti ti-skull fs-4"></i>
      </span>
      <strong>Dogs</strong> – Low sales, low profit (consider removing or reworking)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="fw-semibold">Use this matrix to identify top performers, adjust pricing, and optimize your menu for maximum profitability.</p>
</div>